{
  "id": "02-the-open-door",
  "title": "The Door Is Still Open",
  "tenet": "Fight with the hope of Christ's victory",
  "durationMs": 68334,
  "text": "Imagine a boy who breaks a neighbour's window while playing football. Frightened, he hides behind the shed until evening. His father finds him there. \"I have spoken to our neighbour,\" he says. \"I have paid for the repair. Now come with me. We still need to tell the truth and apologise.\" The boy steps out. The broken window matters. So does the apology. But he can face them because he no longer believes that hiding is his only way home.\n\nThat story gives us a picture of repentance with hope. Christ has already made reconciliation possible. You do not need to pretend that sin is harmless, and you do not need to treat it as stronger than His mercy. Return to God honestly. Make amends where you can. Ask for help where you need it. Your fall does not have to become your home. Fight with the confidence of someone for whom Christ has opened the way back.\n\nIs there something you have been hiding from God, or avoiding putting right? Begin with an honest prayer, then take one step toward repair. The door is still open.",
